{"ts": 0.044877, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;38;5;208m5.1 — print-and-exit vs full-screen\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nMost of the commands you've used print output and return immediately:\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mls\u001b[0m          \u001b[1;38;5;220mdate\u001b[0m          \u001b[1;38;5;220mwc -l file\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nOther commands \u001b[1;38;5;196mtake over the screen\u001b[0m until you exit them:\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mman ls\u001b[0m              \u001b[2m# the manual page for ls\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mless long-file.txt\u001b[0m  \u001b[2m# page through a long file\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mvim file\u001b[0m            \u001b[2m# the Vim editor\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nWhile a full-screen program is running, the shell prompt is \u001b[1;38;5;244mgone\u001b[0m.\r\nYou're inside a program. The same keys may do different things there.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;38;5;244mExit keys\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mman\u001b[0m   →  press \u001b[38;5;208mq\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mless\u001b[0m  →  press \u001b[38;5;208mq\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mvim\u001b[0m   →  type \u001b[1;38;5;220m:q\u001b[0m then Enter (and friends — Lesson 5.3)\r\n\r\nTry one:\r\n  \u001b[1;38;5;220mman ls\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(read a few lines; press \u001b[38;5;208mq\u001b[2m to come back here.)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;38;5", "len": 1024}
